body:
Apologies for taking a while to come back to this!

@beicause Thanks for the feedback. I've added a check for if the image is empty, and added an option to allow overwriting existing files.

@Calinou I've switched the default format to WebP, but PNG is still a supported option just in case. In my opinion this adds a workflow that will be helpful for some users despite the drawbacks. It's simple to understand what it does, so the destructive nature won't be a surprise to users. Realistically I don't have the time or familiarity with Godot to try implementing the caching proposal, so I'll leave it up to you and the other maintainers to decide if this is worth merging. If you do I'm still happy to change to the alternative implementations I mentioned in the PR description!
